# Rules for SMACCS
SMACCS is a CSS methodology for organizing styles into five categories, promoting maintainable and scalable codebases.

## Core Principles

### 1. Base Styles
- What: Default element styles (no classes/IDs)
- Examples: 
  ```css
  body { margin: 0; }
  a { color: blue; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  ```

### 2. Layout (.l-*)
- Use Layouts when creating the *skeleton* of the page, managing how regions are positioned relative to one another
- Rules:
  - Name classes by purpose (not semantics)
  - Use `#ids` for single-use elements
  - Prefer classes `.l-grid` over semantic tags
- Why: Separate layout from content
- Example:
  ```css
  .l-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  ```

### 3. Modules (.module)
- Create a Module for reusable components that don’t dictate page structure but define their own appearance/behavior
- Rules:
  - Self-contained components
  - Avoid element selectors (`h2` → `.card-title`)
  - Variations use sub-classes (`.card-featured`)
  - Designed to function anywhere in the layout
  - Avoid dependency on parent context (e.g., `margin: 0 auto` breaks reusability)
- Example:
  ```css
  .card { /* base styles */ }
  .card-title { /* module child */ }
  .card-featured { /* variation */ }
  ```

### 4. State (.is-*)
- Rules:
  - Toggle via JavaScript
  - Can use `!important`
  - Indicate UI state changes
- Examples:
  ```css
  .is-expanded { max-height: 1000px; }
  .is-hidden { display: none; }
  ```

### 5. Theme
- Rules:
  - Theme overrides via classes
  - Separate theme styles
- Example:
  ```css
  .theme-dark {
    background: #333;
    color: white;
  }
  ```

## Best Practices
- Avoid: 
  - Deep nesting (`nav ul li a`)
  - Semantic layout classes (`.blue-box` → `.l-sidebar`)
  - Table-based layouts
- Organize:
  ```
  styles/
  ├── base/
  ├── layout/
  ├── modules/
  ├── states/
  └── themes/
  ```
- Group properties:
  ```css
  .card {
    /* Box Model */
    display: block;
    width: 300px;
    
    /* Typography */
    font-size: 1rem;
    
    /* Visual */
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
  }
  ```

## Complete Example
```html
<div class="l-container card is-expanded theme-dark">
  <h2 class="card-title">Card Title</h2>
  <img src="image.jpg" class="card-image is-thumbnail">
  <a href="#" class="card-link">Read More</a>
  <p class="card-text">Card content</p>
</div>
```

```css
/* LAYOUT */
.l-container {
  max-width: 1200px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

/* MODULE */
.card {
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 20px;
}

.card-title { font-size: 1.5rem; }
.card-link { color: #007bff; }

/* STATE */
.is-expanded { padding: 40px; }
.is-thumbnail { border-radius: 50%; }

/* THEME */
.theme-dark {
  background: #333;
  color: white;
}
.theme-dark .card-link { color: #a1caff; }
```

## Key Benefits
- ✅ Clear style categorization
- ✅ Reduced selector specificity
- ✅ Theme switching support
- ✅ Team-friendly conventions
- ✅ Scales from small to enterprise projects